MLLM description: Tabby cats are characterized by their distinctive coat patterns, which include stripes, spots, or swirls. These patterns are caused by a genetic trait that affects the distribution of pigment in the fur. Tabby cats can have a variety of colors, including brown, black, orange, and white. The color patterns can vary greatly between individuals, with some having more pronounced markings than others.

In terms of size and proportions, tabby cats generally fall within the average range for domestic cats, neither being particularly large nor small. They typically have a muscular build and a medium-length coat.

Behaviorally, tabby cats are known to be intelligent, curious, and playful. They often enjoy interactive play and can be quite vocal, especially when they want attention. They are also territorial animals and may mark their territory with scent glands.

Unique identifying traits of tabby cats include their distinctive coat patterns, which set them apart from other cat breeds. Additionally, their eyes are often large and expressive, adding to their charm.
