Hogs can vary in color, but common patterns include shades of brown, black, or a mix of both. Some hogs may have white markings on their faces, legs, or bellies. The skin appears smooth and slightly wrinkled, especially around the neck and shoulders.

#### 3. Size and Proportions:
Hogs are generally medium to large-sized animals. They have a substantial body mass compared to their relatively smaller heads and short legs. The length of their body is typically longer than their height at the shoulder.

